@startuml
title seccomp-bpf — filtering a system call

start
:Process issues a system call\n(syscall number + arguments);
if (seccomp filter installed?) then (no)
  :Normal kernel processing; <<#lightgray>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:Kernel runs the attached BPF program\non the syscall number/args;
switch (filter verdict: 8 return values,\ngrouped by outcome)
case (ALLOW, LOG)
  :Execute the syscall\n(LOG also records it); <<#90ee90>>
  stop
case (ERRNO, TRAP)
  :Refuse the syscall:\nERRNO returns an error code,\nTRAP delivers SIGSYS; <<#ffd27f>>
  stop
case (TRACE, USER_NOTIF)
  :Hand the decision over:\nTRACE to a ptrace tracer,\nUSER_NOTIF to a userspace supervisor; <<#add8e6>>
  stop
case (KILL_THREAD, KILL_PROCESS)
  :Kill the calling thread\nor the whole process; <<#ff9999>>
  note right
    Strict mode (mode 1) is the
    degenerate filter: only read,
    write, exit, sigreturn pass;
    everything else is killed.
  end note
  stop
endswitch
@enduml
